.TH CHASHMAP_DESTROY 3 "2026-10-31" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
chashmap_destroy \- destroy a hash map and set pointer to NULL
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chashmap.h>

chashmap_destroy(hm);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Frees everything the hash map holds, all key-value pairs included, and
then sets the hash map pointer to NULL.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
hm   Hash map to destroy (set to NULL after destruction)
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Safe to call with a NULL pointer
Frees all keys and values
Frees every bucket collision chain and the bucket/slot array itself

The macro evaluates hm exactly once. It must be a modifiable lvalue,
such as a variable or an array element, and an expression with a side
effect such as handles[i++] destroys and clears exactly one element.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chmap_destroy (3),
.BR chashmap_create (3),
.BR chashmap_destroy_with_dtor (3)
